#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/reduce_op/index.rst:255
msgid ""
"Must appear exactly once per `T.alloc_reducer` allocation, before any `T."
"reducer_update`. The whole epoch (init, updates, finalize) may sit inside "
"thread-uniform serial loops or conditionals — the epoch then reopens once "
"per dynamic execution — but init and finalize must share the same enclosing "
"loop/branch scope. Without `init`, the reduction starts from the combine "
"identity (sum -> 0, max -> dtype lowest, min -> dtype highest, bitand -> all "
"ones, bitor/bitxor -> 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/reduce_op/index.rst:263
msgid ""
"`init` is a LOGICAL starting value: the result is as if one extra "
"contribution `init` were combined into every logical output, exactly once. "
"It is not a physical fill — physical partials always start from the "
"identity, and the compiler captures `init` at the init site and combines it "
"once per logical output at finalize time, so physical replication can never "
"multiply it and later writes to buffers the expression reads cannot change "
"the epoch's starting value."
msgstr ""

